hi I'm Sal Khan founder of the Khan  Academy and as you may or may not know  Khan Academy is a not-for-profit which  means I don't own it no one does it is a  public charity and it has a mission of  providing a free world-class education  for anyone anywhere and when we say free  we mean free a free world-class  education for anyone anywhere and so  when you hear that you are probably  asking the next obvious question well  then how does all of this stuff get  produced how does Khan Academy exist and  I would tell you that is a very good  question the way that we're able to do  what we do and I want to make it very  clear it's much more than just me making  videos we now have a whole team of 80  full-time people 80 incredible people  some of the most talented people on the  planet in my mind helping to make  content helping to make software helping  to make tools for parents and teachers  and the way that we're able to do this  is through the generous support from  people like you at whatever level that  you might be able to do it this year  Khan Academy has reached nearly 100  million people and if you look at the  number of people we've been able to  reach for the amount of investment  necessary to do it it's pretty hard to  find something with that much leverage  or that much scale you know back in the  day before I worked on Khan Academy  full-time I was an analyst at an  investment fund and in the investing  world you're always trying to look for  the the maximum return on investment if  I invest $100 here and I get a 30%  return  that's better than investing $100  someplace else and getting a 10% return  but in the in the in the charitable  world and the the not-for-profit world  what we think about is social return on  investment and I think you'll find if  you look at the impact that every dollar  donated to Khan Academy helps us reach  five people around the world five people  who will then have access to a free  world-class education that's a pretty  high social return on investment however  much you value this access that these  five new people are going to have and so  in in this time of giving I'll just ask  that you seriously consider Khan Academy  as a place for making your donation and  not only that  the near-term we have a matching grant  program where one of our generous  supporters has offered to match your  donation dollar for dollar so a donation  of $10 will actually allow us to provide  access to a free world-class education  for one hundred students next year so I  don't think there's any other use of a  $10 that that might make you feel better  inside thank you
 

